# Copy to .env and edit. .env is gitignored.
# Loaded by lib/common.sh::bootstrap AFTER the selected VM profile and before
# config.sh. It only fills vars that are still unset, so precedence is:
#   explicit shell env  >  profiles/<vm>.sh  >  this .env  >  config.sh defaults
# (e.g. `SSH_KEY=... ./02_run.sh foo` still overrides everything.)

# Required: path to the SSH private key for the VM. The lab's vm02 and vm03
# share one key, so it lives here (not in the per-VM profiles).
SSH_KEY="$HOME/.ssh/vm_key"

# --- Choosing which VM to run on --------------------------------------------
# VM identity (user/host/port) lives in profiles/<name>.sh, not here. Pick one
# per invocation with the --vm flag (default vm03); every script accepts it:
#   ./01_deploy.sh --vm vm02 <job>
#   ./run_batch.sh --vm vm02 -f batches/standard.txt
# Equivalently via env (the flag wins if both are given):
#   VM_PROFILE=vm02 ./02_run.sh <job>
# To make vm02 the default for this checkout, uncomment:
# VM_PROFILE=vm02

# --- Optional per-run overrides ---------------------------------------------
# Rarely needed — the profile + config.sh derive everything. Uncomment to point
# at a one-off host/layout. REMOTE_SSD_BASE re-roots every remote path at once.
# VM_USER=vm03
# VM_HOST=143.107.165.250
# VM_PORT=5022
# REMOTE_SSD_BASE=/media/vm03/ssd1T/andrew
# REMOTE_WORKDIR=/media/vm03/ssd1T/andrew/dynamic/dynamic-lmms-eval
# REMOTE_HF_HOME=/media/vm03/ssd1T/andrew/hf_cache
